1
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,614
You have seen the idea.

2
00:00:51,564 --> 00:00:54,476
Now here is VibroVision working.

3
00:00:54,476 --> 00:01:02,015
An ordinary video becomes a measurement of motion, a record of the
evidence, and a clear next step for an inspector.

4
00:01:03,583 --> 00:01:08,868
We start with two recordings of the same fan, without a coin and
with a coin.

5
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:12,710
These are real source videos, not an animation.

6
00:01:14,283 --> 00:01:18,730
OpenCV follows the fan housing and a background reference.

7
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:24,376
Subtracting camera motion helps separate the machine's movement from
movement of the camera.

8
00:01:24,376 --> 00:01:28,062
Small changes are measured across many frames.

9
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:33,698
Spectral analysis separates that motion into rhythms.

10
00:01:33,648 --> 00:01:36,728
A peak tells us where motion repeats.

11
00:01:36,728 --> 00:01:43,751
The full pattern adds context, while the frame rate limits which
frequencies the video can actually resolve.

12
00:01:45,316 --> 00:01:51,413
In this run on AWS, tone amplitude changed by about thirty six
times.

13
00:01:51,363 --> 00:01:54,585
That is a difference between these recordings.

14
00:01:54,585 --> 00:01:57,819
It does not identify a damaged bearing.

15
00:01:59,416 --> 00:02:07,060
For longer recordings with distinct visible parts, the mathematical
model also asks how those parts move together.

16
00:02:07,010 --> 00:02:13,169
It checks whether the observations support a physical model before
attempting to locate a change.

17
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:24,725
The inspection agent uses measurements to choose what happens next:
improve a region, gather a longer window, create evidence, or ask
for review.

18
00:02:24,675 --> 00:02:28,348
This trace comes from a controlled synthetic test.

19
00:02:29,916 --> 00:02:36,722
When the footage is too short, unstable, or inconsistent, the system
can withhold a diagnosis.

20
00:02:36,672 --> 00:02:40,873
A person reviews the evidence before approving a work order.

21
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:47,400
The live app runs OpenCV five on AWS Graviton.

22
00:02:47,350 --> 00:02:51,357
CloudFront provides the HTTPS entry point.

23
00:02:51,357 --> 00:02:56,602
Evidence is stored in private S three, and CloudWatch records what
happened.

24
00:02:58,183 --> 00:03:04,215
The same analysis is available in the Google Colab notebook, with
videos read from Drive.

25
00:03:04,165 --> 00:03:08,959
Sixty automated tests complement the real video demonstration.

26
00:03:08,959 --> 00:03:10,931
Camera footage.

27
00:03:10,931 --> 00:03:13,289
Mathematical checks.

28
00:03:13,289 --> 00:03:15,673
Inspectable evidence.
